default false) the turret hands its beam polyline to the level's `WaterManager.boil_along_beam(points, delta)` each physics frame (manager looked up lazily). Boiling needs both flags: `boils_water` here and `boilable` on the `WaterBasin` (default false). The beam has no collision with liquid, so the manager tests it against the basin's liquid polygons; the first point it enters the liquid (or its first point, if it starts inside) is the crossing. A boiled basin emits steam there through `emit_steam()` (`BOIL_STEAM_VOLUME_PER_SEC` per second of contact, independent of any scalar) and loses `BOIL_DRAIN_VOLUME_PER_SEC` × the basin's `boil_volume_scale` × delta through `remove_volume()`. Slag is never boiled (read from the basin's runtime liquid), liquid sealed under a crust it touches is skipped, and a crust stops the beam as before. A pool a faucet refills settles where the beam meets the surface. Glass blocks the steam like any solid tile. The sound `traps/laser_boil` (in `Audio.PLANNED`) plays at the turret when a beam starts boiling something.
